1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,311
If university were a game, I didn't begin with a perfect plan.
如果把大学看作一场游戏，我并没有带着完美的计划开始。

2
00:00:06,633 --> 00:00:09,331
I had to discover my own way forward.
我需要自己找到前进的方向。

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,891
That changed in my first-year C programming class.
大一的那节 C 语言课，带来了改变。

4
00:00:14,082 --> 00:00:20,679
Writing code felt like building with blocks: a few simple pieces could become something that actually worked.
写代码像搭积木，简单的模块也能组成真正运行的程序。

5
00:00:21,061 --> 00:00:22,758
I wanted to keep building.
我想继续探索下去。

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,329
Finishing top of my cohort in that class gave me confidence.
那门课的专业第一，给了我信心。

7
00:00:28,801 --> 00:00:33,807
When the chance came to change my degree, I chose to follow my interest in computing.
转专业的机会到来时，我选择追随对计算机的兴趣。

8
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,909
A university development programme gave me guidance.
学校的人才培养计划，为我提供了指引。

9
00:00:39,358 --> 00:00:44,244
Like finding a walkthrough in a game, it helped me see what might come next.
就像找到了一份游戏攻略，让我看到了下一步的可能。

10
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:51,024
But progress came from putting that guidance into practice, one problem at a time.
而真正的进步，来自把指引付诸实践，逐一解决问题。

11
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:54,428
Mathematical modelling tested that resolve.
数学建模，考验着这份决心。

12
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:59,344
When an approach failed, we checked our assumptions and tried again.
方法行不通时，我们重新检查假设，再尝试一次。

13
00:00:59,787 --> 00:01:03,248
Failure wasn't game over. It was a reason to rethink.
失败并不是游戏结束，而是提醒我们重新思考。

14
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:11,812
Those long sessions taught me patience: to stay with a difficult problem, and keep working towards an answer.
那些长时间的探索教会了我耐心：面对难题，坚持寻找答案。

15
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:16,739
The awards brought confidence.
收获的奖项，给了我信心。

16
00:01:17,224 --> 00:01:23,118
Each felt like another star collected, a small sign that the effort was paying off.
每一份荣誉都像收集到的一颗星，见证着努力带来的进步。

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,439
Missing a scholarship reminded me that confidence also needs careful preparation.
与奖学金失之交臂，也提醒我：信心之外，还需要充分准备。

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,624
Working with the science society taught me to organise a team and learn from others.
理化学社的经历，让我学会组织团队，也向他人学习。

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,427
Then came the next step.
接下来，是新的选择。

20
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:45,167
I chose postgraduate study in robotics at the University of Manchester.
我选择前往曼彻斯特大学，继续学习机器人学。

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,638
The eight stars marked my progress.
八颗星，记录了我的成长。

22
00:01:49,123 --> 00:01:53,259
Behind each one were decisions, setbacks, and another attempt.
每一颗背后，都有选择、挫折，以及再一次尝试。

23
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:02,190
My teammates and tutors helped me find my way, offering ideas, encouragement, and guidance when I needed it.
一路上，队友与导师的想法、鼓励和指引，帮助我找到方向。

24
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,330
There was no ready-made route through university.
大学没有一条现成的通关路线。

25
00:02:06,723 --> 00:02:11,190
I found mine by trying, learning, and choosing to keep going.
我在尝试、学习和坚持中，走出了自己的路。

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,589
I started without a clear direction.
最初，我没有清晰的方向。

27
00:02:15,091 --> 00:02:17,440
Now I'm ready for the next chapter.
现在，我已准备好开启新的篇章。
